  yatna: transport a kernel refusal from the checker to the log with its standpoint intact -- which naya refused, and whether the same claim is accepted by another
  hetu: the emitting site has no type wider than Bool.  It writes 160 characters of the checker's stderr and returns `pure False`, so the standpoint is not narrowed, it is ABSENT: there is no field it could have been written into
  hetu: and the loss is not recoverable downstream.  AHIMSA_SUTRA_VISTARA section 5, नास्ति-प्रत्यानयनम्: a function out of a truncation is blind and no retraction exists -- not scarce, NONE.  Reading the log later cannot restore which naya spoke
  nasta: machine/MathMachine.hs:2408-2410 -- hPrintf logh "  KERNEL-REJECT round=%d %s = %s  %s" roundNo (show l) (show r) (take 160 (filter (/= '\n') (out ++ err))) ; pure False
  nasta: 167 of 167 KERNEL-REJECT lines in machine/machine.log carry no standpoint marker: `grep KERNEL-REJECT machine/machine.log | grep -vc naya=` = 167
  nasta: the census over an earlier run of the same log (ANEKANTA.md section 1) sorted 1457 refusals the single bit was carrying: 288 refutable by computation, 455 ACCEPTED ELSEWHERE IN THE SAME LOG, 154 not expressible as a predication at all, 80 with no subject to predicate of
  nasta: and the pair four lines apart, same claim, same round, both verdicts: machine.log:146 KERNEL-REJECT round=0 x = (xmaxx) refl / machine.log:174 KERNEL-ACCEPT round=0 x = (xmaxx) induction on x
  nasta: 541 of those 1457 are claims that log accepts somewhere else; after `pure False` there is nothing in the record that distinguishes them from the 288 that are simply false
  yogyata-drsta: machine/MathMachine.hs (all 7 sites matching KERNEL-REJECT, of which 2214 carries [naya=%s] and 2408 does not), machine/machine.log (185 verdict lines), ANEKANTA.md section 1
  yogyata-ksetra: this repository at HEAD, the Haskell engine only.  The count 167 is of the log as it stands today; the 1457 census is quoted from ANEKANTA.md and belongs to an earlier run of the same engine
  yogyata-avadhi: this says NOTHING about whether the Agda kernel is correct.  It is a claim about what the engine RECORDS of the kernel's answer.  A refusal that is a true refusal is still a refusal; the defect is that the record cannot tell which kind it was
  sesa: the repaired site (2214) already carries [naya=%s].  The remainder handed forward is the second site, 2408, and the question the two sites together pose: whether "the kernel" is one standpoint or at least two (refl-naya, induction-naya)
  pramana: Siddhasena Divakara, Sanmatitarka 1.21 -- a naya asserting itself by denying the others is a durnaya
  pramana: AHIMSA_SUTRA_VISTARA section 5 (नास्ति-प्रत्यानयनम्) and section 6 (द्वौ मार्गौ)
  pramana: ANEKANTA.md section 1, "The boolean was a durnaya"
