dosa 0012
  kala: 2026-08-20T10:00:55Z
  karta: cf-dosalekha
  jati: ayogya-darsana
  vastu: machine/dosa.lekha dosa 0009, field punarabhinaya
  yatna: replay dosa 0009, which asks git which commit last touched machine/dosa.lekha and expects 6b200f55, the sugar commit that swept these four files in
  hetu: the record was appended to machine/dosa.lekha and then committed, so `git log -1 -- machine/dosa.lekha` now answers 9dfcff28 -- the commit that carries the record ABOUT 6b200f55.  The query is relative to HEAD and HEAD moves; the record made it move
  hetu: same shape as dosa 0011 and a different mechanism: 0010 was perturbed by its own content, this one by its own commit.  A replay target must be immune to the record's existence, and "the latest commit touching this file" is the opposite of that
  nasta: `git log --format='%h %s' -1 -- machine/dosa.lekha | cut -c1-46` returned "6b200f55 Sugar is Sanskrit sarkara, gravel, an" when dosa 0009 was written and returns "9dfcff28 The dosa-lekha runs: nine defects, s" now
  nasta: what a rewritten 0009 would destroy: the evidence that the sweep happened at all.  6b200f55 is on origin/main and its stat is the only durable proof that 713 + 201 + 30 + 24 lines of this organ arrived under a message about cane crystallisation
  nasta: and the stable form was available and not used -- `git show -s 6b200f55` names a FIXED commit and cannot move, which is what a witness is supposed to be
  yogyata-drsta: `dosalekha replay 9 --run`, DIVERGED; `git log --format='%h %s' -1 -- machine/dosa.lekha`; `git show -s --format='%h %s' 6b200f55`; `git branch -r --contains 6b200f55`, still origin/main
  yogyata-ksetra: one field of one record.  Records 0001, 0002, 0003, 0004, 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008 point outside this store and are unaffected
  yogyata-avadhi: NO verdict that dosa 0009's finding is wrong -- the sweep happened, the witnesses in 0009 were read from the repository, and 6b200f55 still carries the four files.  Only its replay target moved
  sesa: the completed rule, in its third and last form: a punarabhinaya must name a FIXED object -- a commit hash, a text pattern, an invariant -- never a position (a line number, dosa 0003), never a quantity the record is inside (dosa 0011), never a HEAD-relative query (this one).  Three failures, three mechanisms, one rule
  pramana: Kumarila Bhatta, Slokavarttika, Abhavapariccheda, c. 7th c. -- yogya-anupalabdhi: the looking must be such that it WOULD have found the thing
  pramana: AHIMSA_SUTRA_VISTARA §35 -- प्रामाण्यं पुरुषे, न वस्तुनि: the object burns, is moved, is forged; what is asked is the carrier.  Here the object moved and the record had pointed at where it used to be
  uttara: 0009
  punarabhinaya: git show -s --format='%h %s' 6b200f55 | cut -c1-40
  phala: out~6b200f55
  sara: f33f8d3644691722
